# Keep documentation current and below 500 lines

Markdown guides, including agent instructions, READMEs and these rules,
have a hard **500-line limit**. Changelogs are exempt; preserve their full history
and generation. Aim for 150–300 lines, with shorter entry points.
Update current descriptions in place; no progress diaries, duplicate ledgers
or archive overflow files. Run `python3 scripts/check-docs.py`; pre-push checks
the pushed tree. See [documentation policy](../../docs/documentation.md).

Write for people: no literal commit SHAs, binary/compiler addresses, checksum
values or evidence-ID dumps. Explain behavior and decisions; link readable source
when useful and keep machine records in manifests, Git or ignored check output.
